An assert statement is outputed for the comment that starts with "@@@". This comment implies that if the return value is negative, then the last index of x in the old array should be -1.--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_Ret < 0 ? Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 : true);
</code>
In the original code, there is a comment "@@@ If the return value is negative, last index of x in old array is -1". This comment indicates that if the return value from calling "IndexOf" on the array list is negative, then the "LastIndexOf" method should return -1. This condition is encapsulated within a Debug.Assert statement.

There were no other comments starting with "@@@", so no further assert statements were created.--------------------